     The default values in src/Makefile for WINSRC, WINOBJ, and
WINLIB are for building a tty-only binary.  They look like

WINSRC = $(WINTTYSRC)
WINOBJ = $(WINTTYOBJ)
.. a fair bit lower down
WINLIB = $(WINTTYLIB)

If you want to make a binary which supports Qt-only or tty+plus+Qt
(or other combinations like throwing in X11), then you need to edit
src/Makefile and update those three values.  For Qt-only, use
WINSRC = $(WINQTSRC)
etc; for tty-plus-Qt, use
WINSRC = $(WINTTYSRC) $(WINQTSRC)
and likewise for the WINOBJ and WIBLIB settings.

     Note that the default value for WINTTYLIB isn't appropriate
for most linux systems these days; comment out the line which sets
it to -ltermlib and uncomment the one for -lncurses instead.  Also
note that if for some reason you eventually run the `sh setup.sh'
step again, you will replace src/Makefile with the vanilla copy so
you'll need to re-edit it to reinstate any desired changes.


